==English==

===Etymology===
From {{affix|en|oil|cloth}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[fabric]] or [[cloth]] treated on one side with a [[waterproof]] covering, especially one made from [[linseed oil]] etc.; used for [[flooring]], [[tablecloth]]s, kitchen shelves and sometimes furniture covering.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1969|passage=Ignatius pounded a paw into the '''oilcloth''' on the kitchen table.|author=[[w:John Kennedy Toole|John Kennedy Toole]]|title=A Confederacy of Dunces|chapter=9|page=224}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1995|passage=When the Lincolns moved into the White House, it was not furnished, there was '''oilcloth''' on the floor in the State Rooms because of the overflow from the [[spittoon]]s.|author=[[w:Barbara Bush|Barbara Bush]]|title=Barbara Bush: A Memoir|page=346}}

